Midnight Reminder
=================

A Pi extension that gently reminds you to stop working at midnight.
If Pi is busy when the time arrives, the reminder waits and is delivered
automatically as soon as the agent becomes idle, so it never interrupts a
turn in flight.

Files
-----

  midnight-reminder.ts         the extension (runtime wiring + messages)
  midnight-schedule.ts         pure scheduling helpers (no Pi imports)
  midnight-schedule.test.ts    unit tests for the scheduling math
  midnight-reminder.test.ts    integration tests with a fake Pi runtime

Load it
-------

  pi --extension ./midnight-reminder.ts

Commands
--------

  /midnight now       show the reminder immediately (manual override)
  /midnight status    print the current state and next scheduled time
  /midnight off       disable the schedule for this session
  /midnight on        re-arm the schedule

Environment variables
---------------------

  MIDNIGHT_REMINDER_TIME            "HH:MM" local time (default "00:00")
  MIDNIGHT_REMINDER_MESSAGE         custom reminder text
  MIDNIGHT_REMINDER_GRACE_MINUTES   start-up catch-up window (default 120)
  MIDNIGHT_REMINDER_DISABLED=1      start with the schedule disabled

Behavior
--------

1. On session start, the extension arms a single timer for the next
   occurrence of the configured time (default local midnight).
2. When the timer fires and Pi is idle, the reminder is delivered:
     - a display-only custom message is added to the transcript
       (triggerTurn is NOT set, so the model does not start working again), and
     - a UI notification is shown when a UI is available.
3. If Pi is busy when the timer fires, the reminder is held and delivered
   on the next `agent_settled` event, i.e. once the agent is idle.
4. Delivery is recorded per local calendar day, so reloads, resumes, and
   branch switches do not repeat the same night's reminder.
5. If Pi is opened shortly after the target time (within the grace window),
   the missed reminder is delivered once as a catch-up.

Test commands
-------------

  node --test                              run all tests
  node --test midnight-schedule.test.ts    unit tests only
  node --test midnight-reminder.test.ts    integration tests only

Try the catch-up path without waiting for midnight:

  MIDNIGHT_REMINDER_TIME="$(date -d '-2 min' +%H:%M)" \
    pi --extension ./midnight-reminder.ts
